# A widget of one clause whose parameter is a tuple pattern of plain names, the blueprint a
# test builds (Semantics ch. 8: a widget's parameters are patterns, as a function's are;
# a test applies its blueprint to its argument as any line does). conformance/
# sem-ch08-widget-parameter-pattern applies such a widget as a line of `@main`, which
# lowers; as a test's blueprint each name of the pattern reaches the internal error "the
# name `name`, which nothing declares" on prismc-s4 (found by sweep-5 writing
# sem-ch09-host-late-value-above-below-building-if).
# Written by Claude (sweep-5, the prismc run), 12 November 2026; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@Page: fn ((Text, Nat)) -> @unit
fn @Page ((name, count)):
    Ui.Label($text=$"{name}: {count}")                           # 0
    if count > 2:
        Ui.Label($text=$"many")                                  # 1
